<h2>Every example, three ways</h2>
<p>Under each example in these docs are three tabs. <strong>HTML</strong> is exactly what the example renders. <strong>React</strong> is the same markup as JSX — <code>className</code>, style objects, closed tags — and compiles as it is. <strong>Ghost</strong> is the Handlebars it was written in, shown when it uses a partial or a helper. Pick one and every example on every page follows.</p>

<h2>What is in the package</h2>
<p><code>npm run package</code> writes it to <code>package/</code>; the docs site serves the current one at <code>/package/</code>, so a plain page can link it straight from <code>design.imswarnil.com</code>.</p>
