<h2>The React layer</h2>
<p>Most of the system needs no wrapper in React — <code>&lt;div className="im-card"&gt;</code> is a card. The layer adds what a wrapper is genuinely for: the head snippet, starting the scripts, and the few primitives whose variants are worth typing. Written with <code>createElement</code>, so it needs no build step, ships its own types, and is server-safe: only <code>&lt;ImScripts&gt;</code> touches the browser.</p>
<div class="im-table-scroll">
